19.2 The automatic-generation principle

Principle 19.1. All counts reported in the manuscript — claims, sources, links, lineages — must be generated automatically from the master files (the claim ledger, source register, and relation table) at the time of publication. Manual counts are prohibited. Where a count is stated in the narrative, it must be traceable to a generated table or script output.

Principle 19.2. Where the master files change, the manuscript counts change. The revision log records the date and the delta. A manuscript that states a count inconsistent with the master files is defective and must be corrected before circulation.

These principles are stated in the manuscript because the v1.0 inconsistency arose precisely from manual counting. The framework's credibility depends on applying its own discipline to its own bookkeeping.

