APPENDIX P — GLOSSARY

Term Definition
Claim A bounded falsifiable proposition about a specific contribution, event, relationship, or outcome (§6.2).
Layer A–H The eight analytical contribution layers (§6.1): knowledge/precursors, conception/design, demonstration/disclosure, engineering/manufacturability, institutional/resource, standards/law/policy, production/diffusion/access, human outcomes/externalities.
Lineage The chain of origin and reuse through which a claim or quotation circulates; sources in one lineage are not independent (§7.2).
CC Chronology confidence, 1–4 (§8.1).
AC Attribution confidence, 1–4 (§8.1).
IE Impact evidence, 0–4; a descriptive indicator of the type of outcome evidence, not its quality (§8.1, §11.1).
MQ Methodological quality of outcome evidence, 1–4 (§11.2).
POP Population specification for an outcome claim (§11.2).
DIST Distributional profile of benefits/harms (§11.2).
CU Causal uncertainty statement (§11.2).
k Number of distinct independence lineages among supporting links with R ≥ 2 (Appendix E, Rule E.1).
C_gen General independence cap = min(4, 2+k) (§8.2).
C_anti Anti-inflation cap = 1 if k=0; 2 if k=1; 4 if k≥2 (§8.2).
C_max Effective cap = min(C_gen, C_anti) (§8.2).
Indeterminate Label applied when CC = 1 or AC = 1; records absence of support, not presence of contrary evidence (§8.3 R5).
"Not established" The current record does not justify a date or conclusion; a research task, not evidence against the claim (§7.3).
"Not applicable" The field genuinely does not apply to the claim (§7.3).
E1–E5 Category, evidence, attribution, impact, and synthesis collapse (§2).
AC-1…AC-13 Audit-completion criteria (§25).
R, P, I, L, D Probative profile dimensions: direct relevance, archival proximity, institutional interest, locator precision, independence group (§9.1).
Reproduction Reviewer-with-packet re-derivation within one band (§12.1).
Pre-registration Public deposit of hypotheses, claims, and analysis plan before the review is run (§12.5; Appendix O).
Synthesis claim A causal meta-claim that must be decomposed into testable components before IE > 1 (§10.5).

